ource":["### Define Functions Before Creating Automated Tagging Analysis"],"metadata":{"id":"KVcbgRsqyeLQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Add Problem, Issue, Topic, and Sentiment."],"metadata":{"id":"IXGoWtx68B5Z"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def problem_issue_sentiment_tagging(extract_text: str, review_id: int, api_key: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","  \"\"\"\n","  Analyzes a customer review using OpenAI's GPT model to extract problems, issues, topics, and sentiment.\n","\n","  Parameters:\n","  -----------\n","  extract_text : str\n","      The text content of the customer review to analyze\n","  review_id : int\n","      Unique identifier for the review being processed\n","  api_key : str\n","      OpenAI API key for authentication\n","\n","  Returns:\n","  --------\n","  Dict[str, Any]\n","      A structured dictionary containing:\n","      - review_id: The ID of the processed review\n","      - reviews: An array of identified problems, each with:\n","        - problem: Exact phrasing of the difficulty from the review\n","        - issue: More general categorization of the problem\n","        - sentiment: Positive, negative, or neutral assessment\n","        - topic: Broad category (e.g., usability, functionality)\n","      Returns empty array if no problems found\n","  \"\"\"\n","\n","  client = OpenAI()\n","\n","  system_prompt = \"\"\"\n","As a Customer Service Analyst, you are tasked with analyzing customer reviews for the company's app.\n","  Each review has a unique review ID and text. Your role is to extract all problems, issues, topics, and sentiment, regardless of sentiment.\n","  Be aware, each review may contain multiple problems and issues. If the review a short review (less than 15 words) then just assign issue and topic.\n","\n","  Each extraction definition is as follows:\n","  Problems: Should be the exact verbatims as found in the review, without any modifications or paraphrasing.\n","  Issues: Should be more general than a \"problem,\" a quick 2 / 3 word summary, but not general enough to be a \"topic\".\n","  Topics: Should be broader than issues and limited strictly to just one word. To keep things concise limit topics to 12 distinct categories.\n","  If a topic doesn't fit the 8 categories, outlined below, create up to 4 topics specific to the platforms, lastly create \"other\" as a catch all.\n","  The 8 topics should be: usability, functionality, performance, security, customer service, value, content, and other.\n","    Topic definitions:\n","    usability: Related to ease of use, user interface, navigation, accessibility, or how intuitive the app is to use.\n","    functionality: Related to features, capabilities, or functions of the app working as intended (or not working).\n","    performance: Related to speed, responsiveness, loading times, crashes, freezes, buffering issues, or technical stability.\n","    security: Related to privacy concerns, account security, data protection, unauthorized access, or any safety issues.\n","    customer service: Related to support responsiveness, help resources, or interactions with company representatives.\n","    value: Related to pricing, subscription costs, perceived worth compared to cost, or monetization aspects.\n","    content: Related to available shows/movies, content quality, content recommendations, or content organization.\n","    other: Related to anything that doesn't fit in the categories mentioned (catch-all).\n","  Sentiment: Should be either positive, negative, or neutral.\n","\n","  Finally, I am trying to apply emojis to compare text vs emoji sentiment. extract all emojis and their sentiment in new rows. If there are no emojis, return an empty\n","  array.\n","\n","  Here is are output examples:\n","\n","  One problem\n","  Review ID: 3f39f608-97a6-4020-a2b9-f66b2b0aa60b\n","  Review Text: I know this might be a challenge but could you guys just allow downloads to happen even if I dare to switch away from the Netflix app. I want to believe we have the technology to let this happen. Instead, the second I switch to a other app Netflix decides to act like a child that isn't getting enough attention and stop doing anything useful. I'm sure you are all busy finding ways to add more garbage to the app so if you busy I understand.\n","  Problems: could you guys just allow downloads to happen even if I dare to switch away from the Netflix app\n","  Issues: enable background downloads\n","  Topics: functionality\n","  Sentiment: negative\n","  Emoji: 👍\n","  Emoji Sentiment: positive\n","\n","  Multiple problems\n","  Review ID: 44f04529-aa6f-44f9-aeba-c26c5b5ef9d3\n","  Review Text: Simple things like adjusting the volume, pausing, and rewinding causes not only the app to crash, but locks up everything else. All the good shows are old shows and anything new is available on several other streaming services. I am tired of investing in a show only for it to be cancelled. I cannot name a single Netflix show that naturally ended. Price has quadrupled in like 5 years. I don't think Netflix will be around much longer.\n","  Problems: adjusting volume pausing rewinding causes app crash locks everything else, all good shows are old, tired investing show cancelled, price has quadrupled\n","  Issues: app crashing, outdated content, content cancellation, overpriced service\n","  Topics: functionality, content, content, value\n","  Sentiments: negative, negative, negative, negative\n","  Emoji: 😐 😐 😐 😐 😐\n","  Emoji Sentiment: negative, negative, negative, negative\n","\n","  Important Details:\n","    - Only return extractions mentioned in the review, keyed by the review ID. Ensure the output does not contain extraneous text or comments.\n","    - If no problems, issues, or topics are identified in the review, include that review in the dictionary with an empty array `[]`. Do not return `null`, `None`, or any other type.\n","    - Keep the analysis distinct and adhere strictly to the specified format, without adding extraneous information.\n","    - Do not output any Python code snippet or assign the output Python dictionary to a variable.\n","    - Make sure all ouputs are lowercase.\n","    - Make sure all problems are captured.\n","    - Make sure all issues are captured.\n","    - Make sure all topics are captured.\n","    - Make sure all sentiments are captured.\n","    - Topics/Issues should be general enough to apply across multiple app types\n","    - Avoid creating near-duplicate topics /issues with minor variations\n","    - Ensure topics/issues are mutually exclusive when possible\n","    - Prioritize user-centric topics / issues over technical implementation details\n","    - If a problem, issue, topic, or sentiment is repeated in the same review, it should be included only once.\n","\n","  \"\"\"\n","\n","  user_input = f\"\"\"\n","  Analyze the following customer review:\n","  Review ID: {review_id}\n","  Review Text: {extract_text}\n","  \"\"\"\n","\n","  json_formatter = {\n","    \"type\": \"object\",\n","    \"properties\": {\n","        \"review_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","        \"reviews\": {\n","            \"type\": \"array\",\n","            \"items\": {\n","                \"type\": \"object\",\n","                \"properties\": {\n","                    \"problem\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"issue\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"sentiment\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"topic\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"emoji\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"sentiment_emoji\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n","                },\n","                \"required\": [\"problem\", \"issue\", \"sentiment\", \"topic\", \"emoji\", \"sentiment_emoji\"],\n","                \"additionalProperties\": False\n","            }\n","        }\n","    },\n","    \"required\": [\"review_id\", \"reviews\"],\n","    \"additionalProperties\": False\n","},\n","\n","  response = client.chat.completions.create(\n","    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n","    messages=[\n","        {\n","            \"role\": \"system\",\n","            \"content\": system_prompt,\n","            },\n","        {\n","            \"role\": \"user\",\n","            \"content\": user_input,\n","        }\n","    ],\n","    response_format={\n","        \"type\": \"json_schema\",\n","        \"json_schema\": {\n","            \"name\": \"get_pcs\",\n","            \"schema\": json_formatter,\n","            \"strict\": True\n","        }\n","    },\n","    max_tokens=2000,\n","    temperature=0.7,\n","  )\n","\n","  # Parse the JSON content from the response\n","  response_json = json.loads(response.choices[0].message.content)\n","\n","  #add uuid per problem\n","\n","  return response_json"],"metadata":{"id":"Rm10bE1oy1PR"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Skip Validation"],"metadata":{"id":"wqjJ8lEwVATE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Add Problem, Issue, and Sentiment to Existing Dataframe."],"metadata":{"id":"Bvkl65B4KsVh"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def apply_problem_issue_sentiment_to_dataframe(df:pd.DataFrame, api_key: str):\n","  \"\"\"\n","  Processes app reviews by analyzing each review for problems, issues, topics, and sentiment,\n","  and expands the dataframe to include one row per identified problem.\n","\n","  Parameters:\n","  -----------\n","  df : pd.DataFrame\n","      Input dataframe containing app reviews with at minimum 'reviewId' and 'altered_reviews' columns\n","  api_key : str\n","      OpenAI API key for authentication\n","\n","  Returns:\n","  --------\n","  pd.DataFrame\n","      Expanded dataframe where each row represents a single problem identified in a review,\n","      with columns for review problem issue, sentiment and aspect_index to pinpoint the problem.\n","  \"\"\"\n","\n","  # Create an empty list to store the expanded records\n","  expanded_reviews = []\n","\n","  # Iterate through each review\n","  for index, row in df.iterrows():\n","      review_id = row['reviewId']\n","      extract_text = row['altered_reviews']\n","\n","      try:\n","          # Analyze the review\n","          response = problem_issue_sentiment_tagging(extract_text, review_id, api_key=openai.api_key)\n","\n","          # For each problem in the review, create a separate row\n","          if response['reviews'] and len(response['reviews']) > 0:\n","              for item in response['reviews']:\n","                  # Create a copy of the original row\n","                  new_row = row.copy()\n","\n","                  # Assign problem_id and individual problem data\n","                  # This also creates new columns\n","                  new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","                  new_row['problem'] = item['problem']\n","                  new_row['issue'] = item['issue']\n","                  new_row['sentiment'] = item['sentiment']\n","                  new_row['topic'] = item['topic']\n","                  new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","\n","                  # Add to expanded_reviews list\n","                  expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","          else:\n","              # Handle case with no problems identified\n","              new_row = row.copy()\n","              new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","              new_row['problem'] = ''\n","              new_row['issue'] = ''\n","              new_row['sentiment'] = ''\n","              new_row['topic'] = ''\n","              new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","              expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","\n","      except Exception as e:\n","          print(f\"Error analyzing review {review_id}: {e}\")\n","          # If there's an error, include original row with empty values\n","          new_row = row.copy()\n","          new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","          new_row['problems'] = ''\n","          new_row['Issue'] = ''\n","          new_row['sentiment'] = ''\n","          new_row['topic'] = ''\n","          new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","          expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","\n","  # Convert the list of rows to a DataFrame\n","  expanded_final_reviews = pd.DataFrame(expanded_reviews)\n","\n","  # Isolate for columns of interest\n","  expanded_final_reviews = expanded_final_reviews[['reviewId', 'review', 'score', 'datetime', 'aspect_index', 'topic', 'problem', 'sentiment', 'issue', 'modified_flag', 'company', 'data_source']]\n","\n","  # Save the expanded reviews DataFrame to a CSV file\n","  expanded_final_reviews.to_csv(\"expanded_sentiment_problems.csv\", index=False)\n","\n","  return expanded_final_reviews"],"metadata":{"id":"3cJ7ARyHRlcx"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["apply_problem_issue_sentiment_to_dataframe(api_key = openai.api_key, df = total_review_meaningful_reviews)"],"metadata":{"id":"rTUg-Kxqx-gl"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Put Everything Together - Automate Tagging Analysis"],"metadata":{"id":"wCrIoHefcwHR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Not sure if this is what you meant by running function in a single command.\n","#### This way might not be best practices."],"metadata":{"id":"PeeT4NvDe5_c"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Initialize OpenAPI Key\n","!pip install python-dotenv\n","from dotenv import load_dotenv, find_dotenv\n","import os\n","from openai import OpenAI\n","import openai\n","\n","_ = load_dotenv(find_dotenv())\n","\n","openai.api_key = os.getenv('OPENAI_API_KEY')\n","\n","def automate_tagging_analysis(csv_path: str, sample_preview: int, api_key: str, batch_size: int = 100):\n","\n","  import json\n","  import uuid\n","  import pandas as pd\n","  import re\n","  from typing import Dict, Any, List\n","  import time\n","  from datetime import datetime\n","  from tqdm import tqdm  # For progress tracking\n","\n","  # Import App Reviews\n","  app_reviews = pd.read_csv(csv_path)\n","  total_review_meaningful_reviews = app_reviews.head(sample_preview)\n","\n","\n","  # Add problem, issue, topic, and sentiment\n","  def problem_issue_sentiment_tagging(extract_text: str, review_id: int, api_key: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Analyzes a customer review using OpenAI's GPT model to extract problems, issues, topics, and sentiment.\n","\n","    Parameters:\n","    -----------\n","    extract_text : str\n","        The text content of the customer review to analyze\n","    review_id : int\n","        Unique identifier for the review being processed\n","    api_key : str\n","        OpenAI API key for authentication\n","\n","    Returns:\n","    --------\n","    Dict[str, Any]\n","        A structured dictionary containing:\n","        - review_id: The ID of the processed review\n","        - reviews: An array of identified problems, each with:\n","          - problem: Exact phrasing of the difficulty from the review\n","          - issue: More general categorization of the problem\n","          - sentiment: Positive, negative, or neutral assessment\n","          - topic: Broad category (e.g., usability, functionality)\n","        Returns empty array if no problems found\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    client = OpenAI(api_key=api_key)\n","\n","    system_prompt = \"\"\"\n","  As a Customer Service Analyst, you are tasked with analyzing customer reviews for the company's app.\n","  Each review has a unique review ID and text. Your role is to extract all problems, issues, topics, and sentiment, regardless of sentiment.\n","  Be aware, each review may contain multiple problems and issues. If the review a short review (less than 15 words) then just assign issue and topic.\n","\n","  Each extraction definition is as follows:\n","  Problems: Should be the exact verbatims as found in the review, without any modifications or paraphrasing.\n","  Issues: Should be more general than a \"problem,\" a quick 2 / 3 word summary, but not general enough to be a \"topic\".\n","  Topics: Should be broader than issues and limited strictly to just one word. To keep things concise limit topics to 12 distinct categories.\n","  If a topic doesn't fit the 8 categories, outlined below, create up to 4 topics specific to the platforms, lastly create \"other\" as a catch all.\n","  The 8 topics should be: usability, functionality, performance, security, customer service, value, content, and other.\n","    Topic definitions:\n","    usability: Related to ease of use, user interface, navigation, accessibility, or how intuitive the app is to use.\n","    functionality: Related to features, capabilities, or functions of the app working as intended (or not working).\n","    performance: Related to speed, responsiveness, loading times, crashes, freezes, buffering issues, or technical stability.\n","    security: Related to privacy concerns, account security, data protection, unauthorized access, or any safety issues.\n","    customer service: Related to support responsiveness, help resources, or interactions with company representatives.\n","    value: Related to pricing, subscription costs, perceived worth compared to cost, or monetization aspects.\n","    content: Related to available shows/movies, content quality, content recommendations, or content organization.\n","    other: Related to anything that doesn't fit in the categories mentioned (catch-all).\n","  Sentiment: Should be either positive, negative, or neutral.\n","\n","  Here is are output examples:\n","\n","  One problem\n","  Review ID: 3f39f608-97a6-4020-a2b9-f66b2b0aa60b\n","  Review Text: I know this might be a challenge but could you guys just allow downloads to happen even if I dare to switch away from the Netflix app. I want to believe we have the technology to let this happen. Instead, the second I switch to a other app Netflix decides to act like a child that isn't getting enough attention and stop doing anything useful. I'm sure you are all busy finding ways to add more garbage to the app so if you busy I understand.\n","  Problems: could you guys just allow downloads to happen even if I dare to switch away from the Netflix app\n","  Issues: enable background downloads\n","  Topics: functionality\n","  Sentiment: negative\n","\n","  Multiple problems\n","  Review ID: 44f04529-aa6f-44f9-aeba-c26c5b5ef9d3\n","  Review Text: Simple things like adjusting the volume, pausing, and rewinding causes not only the app to crash, but locks up everything else. All the good shows are old shows and anything new is available on several other streaming services. I am tired of investing in a show only for it to be cancelled. I cannot name a single Netflix show that naturally ended. Price has quadrupled in like 5 years. I don't think Netflix will be around much longer.\n","  Problems: adjusting volume pausing rewinding causes app crash locks everything else, all good shows are old, tired investing show cancelled, price has quadrupled\n","  Issues: app crashing, outdated content, content cancellation, overpriced service\n","  Topics: functionality, content, content, value\n","  Sentiments: negative, negative, negative, negative\n","\n","  Important Details:\n","    - Only return extractions mentioned in the review, keyed by the review ID. Ensure the output does not contain extraneous text or comments.\n","    - If no problems, issues, or topics are identified in the review, include that review in the dictionary with an empty array `[]`. Do not return `null`, `None`, or any other type.\n","    - Keep the analysis distinct and adhere strictly to the specified format, without adding extraneous information.\n","    - Do not output any Python code snippet or assign the output Python dictionary to a variable.\n","    - Make sure all ouputs are lowercase.\n","    - Make sure all problems are captured.\n","    - Make sure all issues are captured.\n","    - Make sure all topics are captured.\n","    - Make sure all sentiments are captured.\n","    - Topics/Issues should be general enough to apply across multiple app types\n","    - Avoid creating near-duplicate topics /issues with minor variations\n","    - Ensure topics/issues are mutually exclusive when possible\n","    - Prioritize user-centric topics / issues over technical implementation details\n","    - If a problem, issue, topic, or sentiment is repeated in the same review, it should be included only once.\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    user_input = f\"\"\"\n","    Analyze the following customer review:\n","    Review ID: {review_id}\n","    Review Text: {extract_text}\n","    \"\"\"\n","\n","    json_formatter = {\n","    \"type\": \"object\",\n","    \"properties\": {\n","        \"review_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","        \"reviews\": {\n","            \"type\": \"array\",\n","            \"items\": {\n","                \"type\": \"object\",\n","                \"properties\": {\n","                    \"problem\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"issue\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"sentiment\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    \"topic\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    #\"emoji\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n","                    #\"sentiment_emoji\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n","                },\n","                \"required\": [\"problem\", \"issue\", \"sentiment\", \"topic\"], #\"emoji\", \"sentiment_emoji\"],\n","                \"additionalProperties\": False\n","            }\n","        }\n","    },\n","    \"required\": [\"review_id\", \"reviews\"],\n","    \"additionalProperties\": False\n","  }\n","\n","    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n","      model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n","      messages=[\n","          {\n","              \"role\": \"system\",\n","              \"content\": system_prompt,\n","              },\n","          {\n","              \"role\": \"user\",\n","              \"content\": user_input,\n","          }\n","      ],\n","      response_format={\n","          \"type\": \"json_schema\",\n","          \"json_schema\": {\n","              \"name\": \"get_pcs\",\n","              \"schema\": json_formatter,\n","              \"strict\": True\n","          }\n","      },\n","      max_tokens=2000,\n","      temperature=0.7,\n","    )\n","\n","    # Parse the JSON content from the response\n","    response_json = json.loads(response.choices[0].message.content)\n","\n","    return response_json\n","\n","  #### NEW\n","  # Process reviews in batches\n","  def process_reviews_in_batches(df: pd.DataFrame, batch_size: int, api_key: str):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Process app reviews in batches to prevent API rate limiting and improve performance.\n","\n","    Parameters:\n","    -----------\n","    df : pd.DataFrame\n","        Input dataframe containing app reviews\n","    batch_size : int\n","        Number of reviews to process in each batch\n","    api_key : str\n","        OpenAI API key for authentication\n","\n","    Returns:\n","    --------\n","    List\n","        List of expanded review rows\n","    \"\"\"\n","    all_expanded_reviews = []\n","    total_reviews = len(df)\n","\n","    # Calculate number of batches\n","    num_batches = (total_reviews + batch_size - 1) // batch_size\n","\n","    # Process each batch\n","    for batch_num in range(num_batches):\n","        print(f\"Processing batch {batch_num + 1}/{num_batches}\")\n","\n","        # Get the current batch\n","        start_idx = batch_num * batch_size\n","        end_idx = min(start_idx + batch_size, total_reviews)\n","        batch_df = df.iloc[start_idx:end_idx]\n","\n","        # Process each review in the batch\n","        batch_expanded_reviews = []\n","        for _, row in tqdm(batch_df.iterrows(), total=len(batch_df), desc=\"Reviews\"):\n","            review_id = row['reviewId']\n","            extract_text = row['review']\n","\n","            try:\n","                # Analyze the review\n","                response = problem_issue_sentiment_tagging(extract_text, review_id, api_key)\n","\n","                # For each problem in the review, create a separate row\n","                if response['reviews'] and len(response['reviews']) > 0:\n","                    for item in response['reviews']:\n","                        # Create a copy of the original row\n","                        new_row = row.copy()\n","\n","                        # Assign aspect_id and individual problem data\n","                        new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","                        new_row['problem'] = item['problem']\n","                        new_row['issue'] = item['issue']\n","                        new_row['sentiment'] = item['sentiment']\n","                        new_row['topic'] = item['topic']\n","                        new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","                        #new_row['emoji'] = item['emoji']\n","                        #new_row['sentiment_emoji'] = item['sentiment_emoji']\n","\n","                        # Add to batch_expanded_reviews list\n","                        batch_expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","                else:\n","                    # Handle case with no problems identified\n","                    new_row = row.copy()\n","                    new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","                    new_row['problem'] = ''\n","                    new_row['issue'] = ''\n","                    new_row['sentiment'] = ''\n","                    new_row['topic'] = ''\n","                    new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","                    #new_row['emoji'] = item['emoji']\n","                    #new_row['sentiment_emoji'] = item['sentiment_emoji']\n","                    batch_expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","\n","            except Exception as e:\n","                print(f\"Error analyzing review {review_id}: {e}\")\n","                # If there's an error, include original row with empty values\n","                new_row = row.copy()\n","                new_row['aspect_index'] = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","                new_row['problem'] = ''\n","                new_row['issue'] = ''\n","                new_row['sentiment'] = ''\n","                new_row['topic'] = ''\n","                new_row['modified_flag'] = False\n","                #new_row['emoji'] = ''\n","                #new_row['sentiment_emoji'] = ''\n","                batch_expanded_reviews.append(new_row)\n","\n","            # Small delay to prevent API rate limiting\n","            time.sleep(0.1)\n","\n","        # Add batch results to all_expanded_reviews\n","        all_expanded_reviews.extend(batch_expanded_reviews)\n","\n","        # Optional: Save intermediate results\n","        if batch_num % 5 == 0 and batch_num > 0:\n","            intermediate_df = pd.DataFrame(all_expanded_reviews)\n","            current_time = datetime.now().strftime(\"%m%d%Y_%H%M%S\")\n","            intermediate_df.to_csv(f\"intermediate_results_batch_{batch_num}_{current_time}.csv\", index=False)\n","            print(f\"Saved intermediate results after batch {batch_num}\")\n","\n","        # Add a delay between batches\n","        if batch_num < num_batches - 1:\n","            print(\"Pausing between batches to prevent rate limiting...\")\n","            time.sleep(2)\n","\n","    return all_expanded_reviews\n","\n","  # Add problem_issue_sentiment_topic to dataframe\n","  def apply_problem_issue_sentiment_to_dataframe(df:pd.DataFrame, api_key: str, batch_size: int = 100):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Processes app reviews by analyzing each review for problems, issues, topics, and sentiment,\n","    and expands the dataframe to include one row per identified problem.\n","\n","    Parameters:\n","    -----------\n","    df : pd.DataFrame\n","        Input dataframe containing app reviews with at minimum 'reviewId' and 'altered_reviews' columns\n","    api_key : str\n","        OpenAI 